{"title":"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Of the following five statements, how many are correct?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e245d2d2c3cbbe6ed173df133fdae6f3487ab37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(i) } 20\\% \\text{ of } 40 = 8 \\qquad \\text{(ii) } 2^{3} = 8 \\qquad \\text{(iii) } 7 - 3 \\times 2 = 8 \\qquad \\text{(iv) } 3^2 - 1^2 = 8 \\qquad \\text{(v) } 2(6 - 4)^2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"734\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/8/588e1c179ca96c6e3923de0fc6f021779828b1e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 1 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can just simply verify whether or not each statement is true, and count how many are true:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/294c354961ef6978f7c27163583b1b071d07e843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\% \\times 40 = \\frac{1}{5} \\times 40 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"187\" height=\"38\" />, so the first statement is true\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ffbc99e2825b6f4458b370bae99157e55a79e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{3} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, so the second statement is true\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1dc9fb6eeee3947cbc60dc807ac1ef61a113e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 - 3 \\times 2 = 7 - 6 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"172\" height=\"15\" />, so the third statement is false\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea6a30da702a1b0005f27933eef6374dce6afb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{2} - 1^2 = 9 - 1 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />, so the fourth statement is true\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e2c9b4b209c86ddec7e182e3c8cc6c365149b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(6 - 4)^2 = 2(2)^2 = 2 \\times 4 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"235\" height=\"21\" />, so the last statement is true\n</p><p>Four of these are correct. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a05be2210662118ace8ae33a3e4ce9ffa4bd781e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can also use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abcdaffc2986105cd046597bdbf56729ee97436e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} - b^{2} = (a - b)(a + b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"21\" />, or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Difference_of_squares\" title=\"Difference of squares\">difference of squares</a>, to verify <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98ab87569113fb12e3a1df7a46faffe154d51474.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{2} - 1^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/729ffd0dc9430fd66054f244db79f8f6f26ba75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{2} - 1^{2} = (3 + 1)(3 - 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"288\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a05be2210662118ace8ae33a3e4ce9ffa4bd781e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td